-- title:
--   Function field of the second component as a base-changed stalk
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, $\zeta\in L$ a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L\subseteq L((q))$ obtained as the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$, with $p$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$, and let $K$ be an $A$-algebra compatibly with the tower $A\to L\to K$; let $j\in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((q))$ the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{single}(-1,1)\cdot j_{\mathrm{Num}}$ of the modular invariant. Write $X$ for the two-chart integral model over $A$ attached to $(K,j)$ (the pushout of the two affine charts) with its structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ with an $A$-algebra structure, and let $c_1 : C_1\to\operatorname{Spec} k$, $c_2 : C_2\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral. Assume given $k$-morphisms $i_1,i_2$ from $C_1,C_2$ to the base change $X_k=X\times_{\operatorname{Spec} A}\operatorname{Spec} k$ (commuting with the structure maps to $\operatorname{Spec} k$) which are closed immersions, such that every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, the fibre product $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced and its cardinality is a positive number $n$; assume further a section $\varepsilon$ of $X$ over $\operatorname{Spec} A$, sections $\varepsilon_1,\varepsilon_2$ of $c_1,c_2$ with $\varepsilon_1$ followed by $i_1$ equal to the base change of $\varepsilon$, and an integral weight-one form $w$ of level $M$ over $k$ (a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ with integral $q$-expansion whose reduction over $k$ is nonzero). The conclusion is: for every field $F$ with a $k$-algebra structure, every curve model of $F$ over $k$ (an integral, proper, relative dimension one smooth $k$-scheme together with an isomorphism of $F$ with its function field over $k$ and a bijection between its closed points and the places of $F/k$ matching stalks with valuation rings) whose underlying scheme is isomorphic to $C_2$ over $\operatorname{Spec} k$, and every generic point $\xi$ of $C_2$, if $z$ denotes the image of $\xi$ under $i_2$ followed by the projection $X_k\to X$, and the stalk $\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ is regarded as an $A$-algebra via the germ at $z$ of the structure morphism, then there is an ideal $\mathfrak{q}$ of $k\otimes_A\mathcal{O}_{X,z}$ belonging to the minimal primes of that ring, and an isomorphism of $k$-algebras $F\cong\operatorname{Frac}\big((k\otimes_A\mathcal{O}_{X,z})/\mathfrak{q}\big)$.
--
--   This identifies the function field of the second component of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart model with the fraction field of the base-changed local ring at the image of its generic point, cut out by a minimal prime; the substantive input is generic scheme theory (a closed immersion of an integral scheme identifies its function field with the residue field at the image of the generic point, and the local ring of a fibre product computes as a localisation of a tensor product of stalks). It feeds the passage to valuation rings in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_algEquiv_fractionRing_tensorProduct_of_curveModel_snd_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.exists_valuationSubring_algEquiv_fractionRing_tensorProduct_of_curveModel_snd_twoChartModel_x1_mul) in the analysis of the Igusa-type special fibre of $X_1(Mp)$ at $p$.
